# Costco / WebView sync — debug this FIRST

Before re-debugging Costco login or in-WebView receipt fetch, read
[docs/costco-login-postmortem.md](../../docs/costco-login-postmortem.md). It records the
resolved root causes and the hypotheses already ruled out, so we don't re-litigate them.

## The three resolved bugs (check these before new theories)

1. **`wcs-err` redirect loop after successful sign-in** = stale guest WC session in the
   InAppBrowser cookie jar. Fix: `clearSessionBeforeLogin` (Costco-only) clears cookies +
   cache before opening login. Do NOT add a native Safari User-Agent override — UA bot-scoring
   was investigated and **ruled out** (a clean retry with the same UA succeeds).

2. **5-minute hang** instead of a fast error = loop detector not tripping. Fix: post-auth
   fast-fail in `evaluateLoginLoopDetection` (`authCompletePatterns` + `postAuthThreshold`).

3. **No `webview debug:` lines in backend `/api/dev/log`** = iOS `@capgo/inappbrowser`
   requires an **object**, not a JSON string. Always use the `postMsg(type, payload)` →
   `mobileApp.postMessage({detail:{...}})` pattern (see Safeway). **Never** call
   `mobileApp.postMessage(JSON.stringify(...))`.

## Non-issues — do not "fix"

- `duplicate key ... receipts_order_id_key` during sync is expected idempotent behavior (HTTP 200).
- Repeating `script_run` logs before `ordersandpurchases` are harmless re-injection.

Run `cd frontend && npm test` after any change to these files.
